          "fields": {
            "display_title": "This paper presents a novel ADversarial Meta-Learner (ADML), the claimed first work that tackles adversarial samples in meta-learning. In its core algorithm, a given model is diverged simultaneously by a set of clean  samples and a set of perturbed counterparts, to generate two inner models, which are then meta-updated in an adversarial manner using new sets of clean/adversarial samples.",
